  "why": "The statement asks, for each admissible base b, whether infinitely many base-b repunits are prime. Every prime or probable-prime discovery and proof in the record is one more finite instance in one base, so each is scored instances (F5), including the 2025 R109297 ECPP proof. The proof's Prime Pages status conflict does not matter for scope. A single new prime is not a case: no base's infinitude question is settled by it. I scored Bourdelais's 2009 rate-convergence conjecture none, because it is a heuristic conjecture and settles nothing. Santos–Costa (repunit values are not perfect powers) and Grantham (Goormaghtigh primes) answer different questions, so both are variant. No AI system appears in any event.",
